---
// Internal: exercises the §4.3 grid at every breakpoint. Permanently noindex,
// and deleted once a real page uses the layout in Phase 2.
import Boundary from '../layouts/Boundary.astro';
---

<Boundary title="Layout demo — vrovaris.com" noindex>
  <h1>Boundary layout</h1>

  <div class="row">
    <p class="kernel">18ch track<br />mono, --fg-muted</p>
    <p>
      The narrow track on the left is kernel space and the wide track is user
      space. Between them runs a single 1px rule, painted as a background
      gradient on the container rather than as a border on any child, so it
      spans the whole document and cannot develop a gap where sections meet.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <p class="kernel">960px<br />breakpoint</p>
    <p>
      Below 960px the two tracks stack into one column and each kernel block
      becomes a full-bleed band on the ink ground, bounded by horizontal rules.
      The vertical rule is switched off there rather than rotated.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    This paragraph has no kernel block beside it and is not wrapped in a row.
    The rule continues past it unchanged, and — the part that matters — the
    pairing of every row below it is unaffected.
  </p>

  <div class="row">
    <p class="kernel">tab order</p>
    <p>
      Kernel blocks precede the prose they annotate in the document, so tab
      order and visual order agree and neither is reordered by the grid.
    </p>
  </div>
</Boundary>
